# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# "ONLY WHAT'S USED IN THIS VERSION"
#
# The repo lives inside a working directory that also holds 1.8 GB of source material — vendored
# upstream repos, the raw reference dump, and screenshot output. All of it was load-bearing while
# building and none of it is part of the product. Committing it would put a multi-gigabyte push
# between every future clone and a working checkout, and GitHub rejects single files over 100 MB
# outright, so this is a correctness constraint and not just tidiness.
#
# Each exclusion below states why it is not part of this version.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Vendored upstream repos, READ-ONLY by contract. Reproducible from their own origins, and nothing
# in app/ imports from here — the one piece actually used (gesture-lab) was copied into
# app/src/gesture/ with its MIT license carried along.
_vendor/

# The raw reference dump: the Drive export, extracted archives, wireframe HTML, brand captures.
# Design INPUT, not product. The decisions it drove are recorded in DESIGN-SYSTEM.md and in the
# comments at each call site, which is the durable form.
_refs/

# Screenshot output. Regenerated on demand by tools/shot.cjs; committing them would add a binary
# diff on every visual iteration.
_shots/

# Build scratch.
_build/

# Throwaway probe scripts written while reverse-engineering the GLB and sprite formats. Verified
# orphaned: nothing under app/src, app/electron, package.json, or vite.config.ts references them.
# The findings they produced live in the code and its comments, which is the durable form.
app/.tmp-probe/

# MediaPipe hand-tracking binaries — 40 MB of model + wasm, one file 7.8 MB.
# Hand tracking is DEFERRED by explicit user order along with the three simulations, so by the
# "only what's used in this version" rule these are out. app/src/gesture/ ships and is tested; it
# fetches these at runtime from /vendor/mediapipe/, so the feature works as soon as the binaries are
# restored, and their absence cannot break anything that is enabled today.
app/public/vendor/mediapipe/

# Electron installers. A build output, and at ~160 MB past GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit — the
# TOUCH-ME launcher therefore builds from source rather than downloading a release artifact.
app/release/
app/dist-electron/
